# Decisions log — fieldops-app

Root `DECISIONS.md` is the review artifact. Commit bodies may point at it; they do not replace it.

Law: this file. One document only — no `docs/decisions/` sprawl.

## When to write

Same turn as the choice. Do not defer to handoff.

| Event | Section |
| --- | --- |
| Non-trivial trade-off you would defend in review | §1 Five decisions to defend |
| NativeWind + fieldops-ui package boundary | §2 NativeWind / UI package boundary |
| 409 conflict UX | §3 409 conflict behaviour |
| Deliberate non-build | §4 What we cut |
| First use of an AI tool in a work stream | §5 AI tools used and where |
| Per-feature brainstorm while building | Working notes (below divider) |

## Handoff shape (keep tight / ~one page)

### §1 — Five decisions to defend

Keep **exactly five** entries at handoff. Overflow goes under working notes, then prune.

```markdown
### <short title>
- **Why:** problem or constraint
- **What:** option chosen
- **Rejected:** option not taken, and why rejected
- **How:** paths, ports, commands
```

### §2 — NativeWind / UI package boundary

- **Problem:** what breaks if host wiring or preset is wrong
- **Solution:** npm package, preset, content scan, peers
- **Cost:** concrete trade-offs

### §3 — 409 conflict

What the technician sees; how typed input is preserved; why that choice.

### §4 — What we cut

```markdown
- **Cut:** specific thing not built
- **Why:** reason
- **Rejected alternative:** what was almost built instead
```

### §5 — AI tools

```markdown
- **Tool:** name
- **Where:** what it touched
- **Not used for:** optional honesty
```

